railer  called PC took the gaming world by storm  with its haunting surreal imagery and  shifting geography the game PG promoted  a Silent Hill reboot by hideo kojima an  acclaimed film director Guillermo del  Toro never materialized but the trailer  was enough to galvanize the survival  horror genre with games moving towards  psychological horror dead spaces action  formula was beginning to look well David  the Stars has moved on Glenn Schofield  who created dead space left visceral and  Electronic Arts in 2009 to form its own  company sledgehammer games write Bagwell  lead gameplay designer on dead space and  creative director on dead space to join  Zynga in 2011 where he led the design  team on farmville 2 and steep losses  visceral vice president and general  manager and the lead executive on all of  the dead space game part of the company  in 2015 in other words the people who  made the franchise great in the first  place have left Star Wars inspired by  dead space's popularity Electronic Arts  had dice handed visceral the reins for  the shoot-'em-up battlefield hardline  and from there  visceral main office went straight to  work on an ambitious and mysterious Star  Wars title overseen by uncharted Amy  Hennig that's exciting news for fans of  both Star Wars and visceral but it  doesn't leave much time for dead space  visceral is booked for the next few  years and if there's going to be more  dead space it'll have to wait until  visceral returns from its trip to a  galaxy far far away  or farther away than their usual one  it's a rarity losers  Han Solo's a [ __ ] it lost its way the  first two dead space games our conscious  throw backs the movies like alien with  the schlubby Isaac forced to fight his  way alone through invested combined  spaces the dead space 3 is different and  a conscious attempt to reach a wider  audience Electronic Arts added co-op  multiplayer to the main campaign and a  stereotypically grizzled soldier buddy  named John carbon the tight  claustrophobic levels are replaced by  snow fields and wide open space allowing  a suddenly more nimble Isaac to simply  dodge out of the way a danger and duck  effortlessly behind protected cover in  other words the series loss what made it  special getting it back will be no easy  feat a reboot makes more sense  visceral Star Wars game is still a  number of years away and that doesn't  count extra time that the studio will  spend on post-launch downloadable  content and a potential sequel by that  point it will have been well over a half  decade since the last dead space game  hit confluence even with tacked on  cliffhanger ending from the dlc it might  make more sense for the company to  reboot the franchise with a new  direction and new characters rather than  continue with something that was no  longer working it could be the Dead  Space is officially dead but if the  series is anything like its Necromorph  monsters it will come back to life  before long on second thought maybe it  should thanks for watching click the  looper icon to subscribe to our youtube  channel let's check out all this cool  stuff we know you'll love to  you
 

